+## eventemitter-remove-context
+
+The API provides removeListenersByContext(context): number, removing every registration whose stored invocation context is strictly equal to the argument, across all event names. Return the count of registrations removed, including duplicate functions and once registrations. Respect existing context normalization: listeners registered with omitted or falsy context use the emitter itself; do not redefine on/once behavior. Preserve unrelated listeners and their order, symbol events, eventNames/listenerCount consistency and emitter reuse after becoming empty. Match stored context exactly rather than function identity or truthiness. Expose the API in CommonJS, ESM and declarations. Existing mutation-during-emit behavior is unchanged.
